# Global working rules

This project uses a project-local memory bank and the Global Working Rules.

## Memory bank

Required active files under `memory-bank/`:

- `context.md` — goal, scope, constraints, relevant files
- `spec.md` — requirements, acceptance criteria, expected behavior
- `progress.md` — completed work, current state, validation, blockers, next steps
- `decisions.md` — material decisions, rationale, rejected alternatives
- `archive/` — completed iterations only; do not read unless the user asks

Read the four active files before substantial planning or implementation. Update them after material plans, decisions, milestones, validation, blockers, handoffs, or completion.

## Operating norms

- Check for applicable skills before non-trivial tasks; read full skill files only when relevant
- Make the smallest change that satisfies the request
- Do not commit, push, create branches, or open PRs unless the user asks
- Never expose or commit secrets
- Never claim validation passed unless it was run
- Follow root `AGENTS.md` for HealthCore protected paths and delivery workflow
